    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 1115 PM EDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over Johnetta, or 8 miles east of Mount Vernon, moving northeast at 45 mph. HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph. SOURCE...Radar indicated. IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Locations impacted include... McKee, Donaro, Bummer, Threelinks, Turkey Foot, Robinet, Kerby Knob, Shop Branch, Waneta, Bradshaw, Earnestville, Clover Bottom, Brazil, Hurley, Leighton, Drip Rock, Sandgap, Jep Hill, Blanton Flats, and Delvinta.",
